# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ambient tag chain is inherited by strands spawned via the `,`
#         (fork-detach) separator; tag.stop() on the ambient tag cascades to
#         the parallel strand (row 11 §4.3 + T38 separator runtime).
#
# blocked: compile error — `,` fork-detach separator inside tag-scope body not supported
#   (T39 reason stale; OP_FORK_DETACH guard removed by LANG-S06)
# matrix-row: tag-ambient
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.4 probe):
#   OP_FORK_DETACH transient-strand guard removed (LANG-S06); tag.stop() has
#   been available since M4.  Current blocker: the emitter raises a compile
#   error when `,` appears inside a `t: { expr , expr }` tag-scope body — the
#   `,` fork-detach path in the emitter does not handle the tag-scope nesting
#   context.  Activatable once the emitter supports `,` inside tag scopes.
#
# Urbiscript source (re-activate when , inside tag-scope emitter path works):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var log = "";
#   t: { log = log + "outer", { log = log + "inner" | t.stop() } };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "outer"
